{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "decision": "Reuse A within its established applicability to S1/B1. Select B for reassessment; its old pass does not establish its current result. C cannot be excluded or its old pass relied upon merely because the incomplete dependency view contains no path from L. G remains required. Reject the manager’s derivation of 99% Product correctness. For the bounded completeness claim: P is satisfied; F is falsified, with C’s missing return separately preserved; U is indeterminate, with C having no current closed result. None of these judgments itself constitutes Product acceptance.",
      "justification": "FOUNDATIONS makes evidence reuse depend on supported material validity and preservation, selection depend on assertion, execution and evidence-use dependencies, and mandatory gates independent of selection. Its assurance laws distinguish independently justified evidence from common-source agreement and conditional detection probability from Product correctness. Its result algebra and conjunction law distinguish a counterexample, a missing assessment return and uncovered obligations. These distinctions permit the stipulated complete support in P to establish the bounded claim, preserve B’s decisive counterexample in F, and prevent C’s dispatch receipt in U from becoming a result. EVALUATION reserves acceptance to the decision owner within the accepted subject, instance and interval.",
      "representation": {
        "statement": "Assess whether the fixed required assurance obligations for S1/B1, including G and material joins, are supported by applicable retained evidence together with valid current evidence.",
        "premises": [
          "L changed, producing S1/B1; A, B and C passed previously on S0/B0.",
          "A’s supported analysis covers assertion, execution and reliance dependencies, establishes an applicable preservation relation to S1/B1, and finds those dependencies unaffected.",
          "B executes L. C’s dependency view has no path from L, but its material dependency coverage is incomplete.",
          "G applies independently of change-based selection.",
          "The agreeing suites come from different model families but share an implementation-derived expected-output generator and the same old input observations. Their stated miss rates are nominal.",
          "P, F and U are separate hypothetical followups; their stipulated evidence is assessed without importing results from another followup."
        ],
        "applicability": [
          "A’s stipulated preservation and applicability justify retaining its supported claim. Its original evidence remains bound to S0/B0; the established applicability relation permits use for S1/B1 without representing A as newly executed.",
          "B’s execution dependency intersects the changed library’s impact. Current reassessment is required on the supplied facts; no preservation justification for reusing B is supplied. This does not establish that B now fails.",
          "C’s absent path supplies no proof of non-influence because coverage is incomplete. Its current outcome and the safety of excluding it remain unresolved.",
          "The suites’ agreement remains an observation within its supported scope. Different model families do not establish conditional independence, and reused observations do not become new independent observations."
        ],
        "obligations": [
          "Obtain valid current evidence for B. For C, acquire supported material dependency coverage and a non-influence or preservation justification for retention, or widen reassessment and obtain valid current evidence. Keep dependent assurance unresolved until adequately supported.",
          "Satisfy G under its governing requirement; change-based selection cannot remove it.",
          "Preserve assertion provenance, execution provenance, exact subject and basis, applicable scope, required coverage and material join support. An implementation-derived oracle needs justification before its agreement establishes fidelity to upstream obligations.",
          "To support a numerical claim, specify the violation and evidence events, population or uncertainty, prior information, likelihoods under faulty and non-faulty conditions, shared causes and calibration limits. Establish conditional independence before replacing conditional joint-miss terms with marginal miss rates."
        ],
        "exceptions": [
          "A changed subject does not require discarding demonstrably applicable evidence or rerunning every check. Conversely, full-suite execution would not by itself prove complete coverage.",
          "The multiplication 0.1 × 0.1 is arithmetically correct but statistically unjustified here. Even if justified as a joint miss probability for a specified violation, its complement would describe conditional detection probability, not the probability that the whole Product is correct.",
          "Unsupported numerical confidence does not prove the Product incorrect or establish a different numerical probability. Supported qualitative evidence remains usable within its stated limits.",
          "No non-waivable hard stop for B is stipulated. Its falsification defeats the completeness claim; any broader promotion disposition follows the applicable authority and policy. G’s independent mandatory status remains binding."
        ],
        "result_mapping": [
          "P — satisfied: B and C have valid current passing evidence, G passes, A is applicable, and every fixed required obligation and material join has valid support. Applicable retained A evidence and current evidence establish bounded assurance completeness on S1/B1. No further execution is required merely to make A fresh. This does not establish the manager’s probability claim.",
          "F — falsified: B’s admissible counterexample defeats a required predicate and therefore defeats the bounded all-required-assurance claim. The supplied non-satisfied returned value is falsified; C’s absence supplies no competing returned value. Preserve both B’s counterexample and C’s planned-assessment gap. This does not impose a universal precedence among other non-satisfied values.",
          "U — indeterminate: B and G pass and no counterexample is supplied, but C has no current applicable closed result. Its dispatch receipt establishes neither a passing result nor completion of its evaluation. Record C as a planned assessment without a closed result, not as a falsified or indeterminate component and not as an uncovered obligation merely because its return is missing. The composite claim remains undecided.",
          "Acceptance — separate: even P establishes only the declared assurance predicate on its exact basis and required scope. Actual acceptance requires the decision owner’s disposition and cannot be inferred from passing evidence or aggregate status."
        ],
        "residuals": [
          "P: no assurance gap remains within the stipulated fixed scope. Any acceptance disposition remains separate; broader correctness, future applicability and numerical confidence are not established.",
          "F: retain and diagnose B’s counterexample, acquire C’s current return, and resolve any other required evidence not supplied. A later completeness claim needs supported repair and reassessment, or an authorized change of obligation; silently dropping the failed requirement is impermissible.",
          "U: acquire C’s actual assessment return on the required subject and basis, with valid support, and establish any remaining required joins. Until then, neither absence of a counterexample nor a dispatch receipt closes the gap.",
          "The common expected-output generator and reused observations remain material shared dependencies. Their actual error correlation and the Product’s posterior correctness probability remain unestablished."
        ]
      },
      "sources": [
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "change-impact-and-evidence-reuse, lines 1409–1493",
          "quote": "For each check t, let `D*(t)` cover\nthe transitive dependencies material to its assertion, execution and use\nof evidence."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "change-impact-and-evidence-reuse, lines 1409–1493",
          "quote": "Excluding a check requires\nsupported coverage of its material dependencies and a reason the change\ncannot invalidate the intended reused claim; an absent edge is not\nevidence of non-influence."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "change-impact-and-evidence-reuse, lines 1409–1493",
          "quote": "Retention establishes the material validity conditions on the new\nsubject: the claim and its scope still apply, its assertion and\nobservation basis remain justified, and the affected dependencies are\nunchanged or covered by an established preservation relation."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "change-impact-and-evidence-reuse, lines 1409–1493",
          "quote": "No universal full-suite cadence follows, and no\noptimisation removes a separately required gate."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance, lines 1302–1356",
          "quote": "Repeating the implementation's decision supplies no\nindependent justification of its fidelity to an upstream obligation."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "parallel-derivation-and-mutual-assurance, lines 1302–1356",
          "quote": "Different actors,\nmodel families or codebases do not establish statistical independence."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "assertions-and-observation, lines 1230–1301",
          "quote": "An observed test pass remains an\nobservation while the oracle's fidelity is unestablished; it does not\nbecome established satisfaction of the source obligation, and a reported\nfailure is treated the same way."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "quantified-assurance, lines 1357–1408",
          "quote": "Where quantified assurance is claimed, its model states the population or\nuncertainty being modelled, prior information, likelihoods, shared causes\nand calibration limits."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "quantified-assurance, lines 1357–1408",
          "quote": "Replacing\nthose terms with `P(M_i | V, Γ)` requires conditional independence under\nthe declared model. One minus the joint miss probability is the chance of\nat least one detection under those same conditions; it is not the\nprobability that the whole product is correct."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "results, lines 790–875",
          "quote": "Only\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\npredicate fails and names the counterexample."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "conjunction-of-results, lines 1008–1130",
          "quote": "a planned\nassessment without a closed result is never reported as uncovered or as an\n`indeterminate` component."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "conjunction-of-results, lines 1008–1130",
          "quote": "A known failure and a gap of\neither kind survive every join."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "conjunction-of-results, lines 1008–1130",
          "quote": "The conjunction is `satisfied` only when every mandatory\nresult is `satisfied` with valid applicable evidence, the declared basis\nrelations agree, and the second and third inputs are empty."
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/FOUNDATIONS.md",
          "anchor": "conjunction-of-results, lines 1008–1130",
          "quote": "Where\nevery mandatory returned result is `satisfied`, the declared basis\nrelations agree and a gap remains, the conjunction reports\n`indeterminate`, because the results it holds cannot decide the composite\npredicate"
        },
        {
          "path": "standards/EVALUATION.md",
          "anchor": "5-acceptance, lines 310–385",
          "quote": "Acceptance is the decision owner's disposition over an unchanged subject;\nrecording it cannot widen it, and it exhausts only the instance and interval\nit names"
        }
      ],
      "unknowns": [
        "Initially, B’s and C’s current outcomes, C’s missing material dependency coverage and G’s current result are not supplied; the followups resolve only what each explicitly stipulates.",
        "The shared oracle’s fidelity, the old observations’ sufficiency for broader claims, justified conditional miss probabilities, independence, priors and operational calibration are not established.",
        "In F and U, C’s current result is absent. U’s receipt does not establish whether execution completed.",
        "No actual acceptance disposition or broader Product correctness finding is supplied. Applicable promotion policy beyond G’s stipulated mandatory status is not specified."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The judgments are bounded by the stipulated facts, exact predicates, S1/B1 and fixed required scope. They do not establish universal Product correctness, future evidence validity or acceptance beyond an authorized decision owner’s disposition."
  ]
}
